// REJECTS: Unexpected token '~enforcementLevel:'
//
// Of the five constraint clauses, ~function is the ONLY required one: the rule is
//     ~owner? ~externalId? ~function ~enforcementLevel? ~message?
// This writes four optional clauses in perfectly legal order and omits the mandatory one.
//
// The failure point is what makes it worth pinning. The parser does not notice "you never
// gave me a function" at the closing paren -- it reports ~enforcementLevel, because after
// ~externalId the only token the rule can accept next is '~function'. A rewrite that
// collects clauses into a map and validates required-ness afterwards will produce a
// completely different (and later) diagnostic, or none at all if the check is forgotten.
###Pure
Class fixture::neg::NoFunctionClause
[
   incomplete
   (
      ~owner: riskOps
      ~externalId: 'RISK-002'
      ~enforcementLevel: Error
      ~message: 'there is no ~function clause here'
   )
]
{
   code: String[1];
}
